title: 'statement-store: keep the no-DHT mark only while the peer''s substream is open'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    With the v2 DHT path on, a peer marked as without the DHT path now returns to the DHT index
    when its statement substream closes, instead of staying out until a new substream opens. A
    peer that restarts with the DHT path on is no longer left out of routing and replica choice.
    A peer still without the DHT path is marked again once it reconnects and the grace period
    passes. While its substream is open, a marked peer the node holds reserved stays reserved, so
    the node keeps the connection instead of dropping it.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
